{
  "background_and_question": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Kent E. Cattani",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "b9a45b3f342a51b447d079636af8645d020bdbe8fe94495b9c2ab8c5ab02b5be",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-b9a45b3f342a-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Kent E. Cattani, petitioner argues that the Ninth Circuit's rejection of a State court factual determination is improper under any deferential standard, especially under the highly deferential standard required by AEDPA."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Kent E. Cattani",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "b9a45b3f342a51b447d079636af8645d020bdbe8fe94495b9c2ab8c5ab02b5be",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-b9a45b3f342a-0000-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 12,
              "start": 12
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Kent E. Cattani, petitioner asserts that the State court's determination of the facts was unreasonable."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Respondent (Mr. CATTANI)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "b9a45b3f342a51b447d079636af8645d020bdbe8fe94495b9c2ab8c5ab02b5be",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-b9a45b3f342a-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 22,
              "start": 22
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Respondent (Mr. CATTANI), according to Respondent (Mr. CATTANI), respondent raises the issue of ineffective assistance of counsel."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "b9a45b3f342a51b447d079636af8645d020bdbe8fe94495b9c2ab8c5ab02b5be",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-b9a45b3f342a-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 39,
              "start": 39
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioner, petitioner alleges that witnesses can attest to the use of alcohol and drugs by the biological mother when Landrigan was in utero."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "b9a45b3f342a51b447d079636af8645d020bdbe8fe94495b9c2ab8c5ab02b5be",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-b9a45b3f342a-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 45,
              "start": 45
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioner claims that mental\u2011health expert testimony, if prepared, could have been critically important to the case."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice STEVENS",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "b9a45b3f342a51b447d079636af8645d020bdbe8fe94495b9c2ab8c5ab02b5be",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-b9a45b3f342a-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Stevens asked, \u201cMay I ask about the first one? Does the Constitution require there be no involuntary?\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice KENNEDY",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "b9a45b3f342a51b447d079636af8645d020bdbe8fe94495b9c2ab8c5ab02b5be",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-b9a45b3f342a-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kennedy asked, \u201cIn your view, what is the standard for when the district court may hold an evidentiary hearing?\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice SOUTER",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "b9a45b3f342a51b447d079636af8645d020bdbe8fe94495b9c2ab8c5ab02b5be",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-b9a45b3f342a-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 29,
              "start": 28
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Souter asked, \u201cAre you saying the waiver does not need to be a knowing waiver \u2026 based upon an appreciation of all the possible mitigation evidence \u2026?\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "b9a45b3f342a51b447d079636af8645d020bdbe8fe94495b9c2ab8c5ab02b5be",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-b9a45b3f342a-0002-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 53,
              "start": 53
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kennedy, justice Kennedy noted that the district court has substantial discretion in determining whether to grant a hearing."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "b9a45b3f342a51b447d079636af8645d020bdbe8fe94495b9c2ab8c5ab02b5be",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-b9a45b3f342a-0002-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 42,
              "start": 42
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Ginsburg asked, \u201cCould you do it concretely, Mr. Verrilli, for this case. The defendant is being rather obstreperous and says: I don\u2019t want any mitigating evidence; I\u2019m a really bad guy.\u201d"
      }
    ],
